# Stock market — NIFTY 3PM breakout playbook

This repo contains a **mechanical playbook** (docs) and a **Python backtest** for the late-session 3:00–3:10 breakout idea on **NIFTY 5-minute data** (signals on the index; P&L simulated in **index points**). A **TradingView Pine** helper is under `tradingview/`.

## Install

```powershell
cd C:\Users\arwin\Desktop\Stock_market
pip install -e .
```

## Backtest (CSV)

CSV columns: `datetime`, `open`, `high`, `low`, `close`, `volume` (naive timestamps are treated as Asia/Kolkata).

```powershell
python -m stock_market.cli backtest --csv data\sample_nifty_5m.csv --output-dir out
```

Outputs:

- `out/trades.csv` — one row per trade
- `out/skips.json` — per-day skip reasons when no trade
- `out/metrics.json` — win rate, total/average P&L in points

### Useful CLI knobs

- `--slippage` — adverse slippage in index points (default `0.5`)
- `--reward-r` — target as multiple of risk (default `1.35`)
- `--stop-mode` — `opposite_side` | `half_ref_range`
- `--min-ref-range` — minimum 2:55 candle range (points)
- `--volume-mult` — breakout volume vs rolling average
- `--max-vwap-dev` — max `|close−VWAP|/VWAP` to allow (default `0.012`)
- `--ema-flat-max-slope` — skip if EMA slope (points / lookback) is below this
- `--vwap-chop-max` — max VWAP crossings in lookback window
- `--strict-expiry` — skip on configured expiry weekdays

## Backtest (Yahoo Finance — quick “API” smoke test)

Uses the `yfinance` package (HTTP to Yahoo). **No API key.** NIFTY 50 index symbol is **`^NSEI`**. Intraday 5m history is **short** (often on the order of ~60 days — see Yahoo limits).

```powershell
python -m stock_market.cli backtest --provider yfinance --symbol "^NSEI" --yf-period 60d --output-dir out_yf
```

Optional calendar window (dates are passed through to Yahoo as `YYYY-MM-DD`):

```powershell
python -m stock_market.cli backtest --provider yfinance --symbol "^NSEI" --start 2026-03-01 --end 2026-04-17 --output-dir out_yf
```

Data is normalized to **Asia/Kolkata** bar opens to match the strategy. This is **not** NSE’s official feed; use your broker for production accuracy.

**Why 0 trades with default filters?** Yahoo’s `^NSEI` bars usually have **volume = 0** (index), and many real breakouts fail the **VWAP + EMA alignment** rule late in the day — `skips.json` will show `VWAP_EMA_NOT_ALIGNED`. Volume is auto-ignored when the whole session sums to 0. For a looser smoke test on this feed, add **`--no-vwap-ema-align`** (playbook‑strict mode keeps alignment **on** by default).

**PATH warning from pip:** `stock-market.exe` may install outside your PATH. Call the CLI as `python -m stock_market.cli ...` (as above) or add the printed `Scripts` folder to PATH.

## Data providers

- **`CsvMarketDataProvider`** — local file (used by CLI).
- **`YFinanceMarketDataProvider`** — live download via `yfinance` (`--provider yfinance`).
- **`StubMarketDataProvider`** — placeholder; swap for **Zerodha Kite**, **Upstox**, **Dhan**, etc. by implementing [`MarketDataProvider.load_ohlcv_5m`](src/stock_market/providers/base.py) (return a DataFrame indexed by **IST** opens, columns `open,high,low,close,volume`).

## Docs

- [docs/3pm_breakout_playbook.md](docs/3pm_breakout_playbook.md) — full framework + edge cases + reason codes
