## TradingView

- **Indicator (labels):** [tradingview/3pm_breakout_nifty.pine](tradingview/3pm_breakout_nifty.pine) — paste into Pine Editor (5m, timezone Asia/Kolkata).
- **Strategy (orders / backtest):** [tradingview/3pm_breakout_nifty_strategy.pine](tradingview/3pm_breakout_nifty_strategy.pine) — same chart; **2:55** ref on the **confirmed** 14:55 bar. **Default:** `Stop-at-ref` **ON** → stop orders at ref, armed at **15:00** (active through **15:05**); `process_orders_on_close` is a **compile-time constant** in the `strategy()` call (default **`false`**) so intrabar stops can fill on 5m **OHLC**. **Close-beyond-ref mode:** turn `Stop-at-ref` **OFF** and, in the script, set `process_orders_on_close = true` in `strategy(...)` (TradingView does not allow tying this flag to an input). Brackets after a stop fill use **avg entry** and ref-based SL/TP.

## Disclaimer

Educational only. Not financial advice. Options add gap, spread, theta, and IV risk not modeled in the index-point simulator.
